1. inside a macro with n=7: $with_n
2. at top level, n undefined: $show<n:=2> $inh $inh<n=2> defined(n) $probe
3. args too, inside c=9: $with_c; at top level: $cnt $cnt(5)
4. inherited from a -D param: $inh_d $inh_d<d=2> $inh_d<d=!2>
5. a value starting with !: $show<n=\!x> $show<n= !y>
6. defined skips its own scope: $defined(name) $defined(#id) $defined(d)
